(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). NeMo has no NOTICE file. The
module is a new implementation for strings of that logic: it holds no file of
NeMo, it needs no NeMo or torch package, and it differs from NeMo in the two
places that its module docstring lists.

The module downloads two data files from the Hugging Face repository
Phoonnx/magpietts-multi-357m-unicode, at the copy that the Magpie TTS
checkpoint holds. Neither file is in the wheel.

ipa_cmudict-0.7b_nv23.01.txt is an NVIDIA file of the NeMo tree
(scripts/tts_dataset_files, Apache-2.0). It holds the pronunciations of the
CMU Pronouncing Dictionary, whose licence is BSD-2-Clause with one added
sentence (see scriptconv/phonemizers/_thirdparty/dizione/built/LICENSE.cmudict),
converted to IPA by NVIDIA. heteronyms-052722 is also an NVIDIA file of that
tree, under Apache-2.0.

The Magpie copy of the dictionary has sha256 7ea5c4c2. The copy in NeMo at the
commit above has sha256 dd0927ff. Both have the same size, and they differ
only in the order of the two readings of A: Magpie has the schwa reading
first, and NeMo has the diphthong reading first. The module pins the Magpie
copy.
